# $package_title

A product on the [Synapse SaaS Framework](https://github.com/allandanos/synapse-saas):
auth, tenancy, RBAC, plans, entitlements, usage metering, billing and webhooks
come from the package; this repository holds only the product — a Projects
CRUD to start from. The console runs from the published `synapse-saas-web`
image, white-labelled by `branding/` (no frontend code to build or fork).

## Run everything in Docker

```bash
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up --build                 # postgres, redis, migrate, api, worker, web
```

Console: http://localhost:3000 · API docs: http://localhost:8000/docs.
`migrate` runs both migration branches and `synapse-cli seed` on every `up`.

## Develop locally

```bash
uv sync                                   # installs synapse-saas + this package
docker compose up -d postgres redis        # or point SYNAPSE_DATABASE_URL anywhere
cp .env.example .env
make migrate                              # framework migrations + this product's branch
make seed                                 # permissions, system roles, plan catalog
make dev                                  # http://localhost:8000/docs
make test
```

## Make it yours

Edit `branding/branding.yaml` (every key is documented in the file) and drop
your logo and favicon next to it, then `docker compose restart api worker` —
the console follows within a minute. Check a change with
`uv run synapse-cli branding validate --file branding/branding.yaml`. The
console's name, logo, colours, links, emails and invoice PDFs all read it; see
the framework's `docs/branding.md`. Need more than a reskin? Fork the
console (`apps/web` in the framework repo) and point the `web` service at your
own image.

## Layout

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `src/$package/models.py` | `Project(TenantMixin, Base)` — one line of tenancy |
| `src/$package/router.py` | CRUD: permission-checked, plan-limited (`projects` gauge), audited |
| `src/$package/app.py` | `create_product_app()` = framework `create_app()` + your routers |
| `src/$package/worker.py` | your cron jobs, on the framework's arq worker |
| `migrations/` | an Alembic **branch** (`$package`) that depends on the framework head; run via `python -m $package.migrate` |
| `config/plans.yaml` | your pricing (start from the framework's default catalog) |
| `branding/` | `branding.yaml` + logo + favicon: the white-label kit the API serves to the console |
| `tests/` | run on the framework's public pytest plugin |

## Upgrading the framework

Bump `synapse-saas` in `pyproject.toml`, `uv sync`, `make migrate`, and move
the `web` image tag in `docker-compose.yml` (or `SYNAPSE_VERSION`) to the same
release. Your migrations never touch framework tables; the framework's never
touch yours.
